Question.en:
The joint PMF of $(X,Y)$ is given by $f(x,y)=cxy$ for $x=1,2,3$ and $y=1,2,3$, and zero otherwise. Find:

**(a)** the constant $c$;
**(b)** $P(X=2,Y=3)$;
**(c)** $P(X\le2,Y\le2)$;
**(d)** $P(X\ge2)$;
**(e)** $P(Y<2)$;
**(f)** $P(X=1)$;
**(g)** $P(Y=3)$.

Compute confidence intervals at the 95% level for the means of the distributions from which the following sample values were obtained, assuming the population is normal:

**(a)** $n=100$, $\sum x_i=250$, $\sum x_i^2=725000$;
**(b)** $n=100$, $\bar x=83.2$, $s_{n-1}=6.4$.

Using the Central Limit Theorem, construct normal approximations to each of the following random variables:

**(a)** a Binomial distribution $X\sim\text{Binomial}(n,\theta)$;
**(b)** a Poisson distribution $X\sim\text{Poisson}(\lambda)$.
